        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: drain inbound debounce buffer and followup queues before SIGUSR1 reload",
        "body": "## Problem\n\nDuring an in-process SIGUSR1/config reload, inbound messages can still exist only in debounce buffers or followup queues. Closing the process without flushing those in-memory owners can silently discard accepted message content.\n\n## Fix\n\nThis branch is rebuilt on current main as a focused 13-file change.\n\n1. **Close gateway work admission synchronously.** The existing restart request path closes ordinary admission before the drain starts.\n2. **Run one core-private restart continuation.** `gateway-work-admission.ts` tracks the restart drain as root work and permits subordinate command work only inside that internal continuation (and required continuations reserved while it is live). Ordinary post-drain enqueue still receives `GatewayDrainingError`.\n3. **Flush inbound debounce buffers.** `createInboundDebouncer()` instances are weakly registered. `flushAllInboundDebouncers()` repeatedly sweeps until no live buffer remains, clears each timer, preserves per-key serialization, and does not add teardown requirements to channel implementations.\n4. **Drain channel worker queues.** A core-owned registry counts queued and running `ChannelRunQueue` work. The public queue contract remains exactly `enqueue` + `deactivate`; there is no privileged public enqueue method.\n5. **Drain active turns, followups, and late followup work in order.** The run loop flushes debouncers, waits for channel queues, lets existing active work settle, waits for every followup queue, then rechecks command/embedded work started by followup delivery.\n6. **Count all followup backlog.** `waitForFollowupQueueDrain()` counts `items.length + droppedCount + draining`, so overflow-summary content cannot be reported as drained early.\n\nExplicit forced restarts retain their existing skip-drain behavior.\n\n## Compatibility and security boundary\n\n- Removed the prior `ChannelRunQueue.enqueueInternal` / `allowDuringGatewayDrain` public SDK bypass.\n- No `CommandQueueEnqueueOptions` escape hatch is exposed.\n- `createInboundDebouncer()` keeps its existing public return signature (`enqueue`, `flushKey`, `cancelKey`); its flush hook is symbol-private.\n- `ChannelRunQueue` keeps its existing public shape.\n- The branch diff is now 13 focused files (+635/-127), down from the stale 31-file/+1330 version.\n\n## Exact-head validation\n\n- **PR head:** `5c06769703c80bf306311dac261e0e3cefce402f`\n- **Synchronized main cutoff:** `262baedcf7fa3d66dc35cce7d0253e0a31f0cc0e`\n- **Merge topology:** the cutoff synchronization commit has first parent `da4b1b9c15b6a7b965657fc753e0c25d8dd0e4fa` and second parent `262baedcf7fa3d66dc35cce7d0253e0a31f0cc0e`.\n- Every existing touched main-path blob was re-fetched at the cutoff and verified unchanged from the tested source; the three added paths were verified absent. The 13 changed blobs in the final head are byte-for-byte the locally tested files.\n- **Environment:** Linux 6.12.47, Node v24.14.0.\n\n### Runtime behavior proof\n\nA temporary `tsx` driver loaded the changed TypeScript modules directly and exercised real timers, registries, queue work, and command admission:\n\n```text\n$ node --import tsx proof-pr46303.mts\ndebounce {\"delivered\":[[\"hello\",\"there\"],[\"howdy\"],[\"ping-1\",\"ping-2\"]],\"elapsedMs\":0,\"flushedBuffers\":3,\"secondSweep\":0}\nfollowup {\"result\":{\"drained\":true,\"remaining\":0},\"elapsedMs\":152}\nfollowup-timeout {\"drained\":false,\"remaining\":2}\nchannel {\"pending\":{\"drained\":false,\"remaining\":1},\"drained\":{\"drained\":true,\"remaining\":0}}\nadmission {\"externalError\":\"GatewayDrainingError\",\"internalResult\":\"accepted\"}\n```\n\nThis demonstrates that three 2.5-second debounce buffers flush immediately and only once; a live followup drain waits through `droppedCount` summary backlog; timeout reports the two pending summaries; channel queue accounting observes active work until settlement; and the gateway fence rejects ordinary enqueue while accepting the core-private restart continuation.\n\n### Automated checks\n\n```text\n$ vitest run <six focused files>\nTest Files  6 passed (6)\nTests       166 passed (166)\nDuration    5.90s\n\n$ oxlint --tsconfig config/tsconfig/oxlint.core.json <changed core files>\n(no findings)\n\n$ oxfmt --check <13 changed files>\nAll matched files use the correct format.\n\n$ run-tsgo -p tsconfig.core.json\npassed\n\n$ run-tsgo -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.core.test.json\npassed\n\n$ run-tsgo -p tsconfig.plugin-sdk.dts.json --declaration true\npassed\n```\n\nGitHub Actions is running on the exact head above.\n\n## Not tested\n\nA live Signal account was not paired in this environment, so I did not execute a real Signal → `config.patch` → SIGUSR1 roundtrip. The production restart ordering is covered by `run-loop.test.ts`, and the underlying buffer, queue, admission, and timer behavior was exercised directly as shown above.\n",
